%description:

The standard deviation of the shadow fading of an indoor UE's link, as TR 36.873
and the single-frequency model of TR 38.901 give it: 7 dB. The model deviates:
it takes the outdoor link's value for its LOS state.
ChannelModelIndoorShadowing pins what the model does, so that this test fails on
its checks and not on an abort.

TR 36.873 v12.7.0 7.2.3, rows "3D-UMi O2I" and "3D-UMa O2I": "sigma_SF =7"; the
O2I columns of Table 7.3-6 have the same in "Shadow fading (SF) [dB]".
TR 38.901 v16.1.0 7.4.3.1: "For backwards compatibility with TR 36.873 [3], the
following building penetration model should be used for UMa and UMi
single-frequency simulations at frequencies below 6 GHz.", and in Table 7.4.3-3
the row sigma_SF: "7 dB (note: replacing the respective value in Table
7.4.1-1)".

Checked on a UMa cell with one carrier at 2 GHz -- a single-frequency simulation
below 6 GHz, where Table 7.4.3-3 applies -- on the first shadowing value of the
links of four indoor UEs, under the TR 38.901 and the TR 36.873 channel model,
in LOS and in NLOS. The value is one N(0, sigma) draw; it is divided by the
standard-normal draw replayed from a copy of the model's generator, which gives
sigma. The cases are graded against t901_sigma_o2i_sub6 and t873_sigma_o2i of
pathloss_reference.py.

%expected-failure: an indoor UE's shadow fading has the outdoor link's standard deviation (4 or 6 dB for UMa), where TR 36.873 7.2.3 and TR 38.901 Table 7.4.3-3 give 7 dB

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"
#include "PathLossTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr36873ChannelModel;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        model901: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        model873: Tr36873ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

# one carrier below 6 GHz: a single-frequency simulation
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

**.shadowing = true
**.fading = false
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
auto *model901 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model901");
auto *model873 = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model873");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");

// a UMa base station and four UEs at one place, 100 m from it: a link each, so a
// first shadowing value each
StubEndpoint bsEndpoint;
bsEndpoint.nodeId = MacNodeId(1);
bsEndpoint.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bsEndpoint.nodeId, &bsEndpoint);
StubEndpoint ues[4];
std::vector<std::unique_ptr<StubRadioRegistration>> ueRadios;
for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    ues[i].nodeId = MacNodeId(1025 + i);
    ues[i].coord = Coord(100, 0, 1.5);
    ueRadios.push_back(std::make_unique<StubRadioRegistration>(medium, ues[i].nodeId, &ues[i]));
}
const double d2D = 100.0, d3D = std::sqrt(100.0 * 100.0 + 23.5 * 23.5);

wait(0.010);

// The standard deviation a link's first shadowing value was drawn with: the
// value is one N(0, sigma) draw, replayed here as a standard-normal one from a
// copy of the model's generator, so their ratio is sigma.
auto sigmaOf = [&] (StochasticChannelModel *model, StubEndpoint& ue, bool indoor, bool los) {
    ue.insideBuilding = indoor;
    ue.insideDistance = indoor ? 10.0 : 0.0;
    ChannelModelProbe probe(model);
    RadioLink link = probe.whatIfLink(&ue, dlCqiTransmission(&bsEndpoint, ue.nodeId));
    RngSnapshot snapshot(model);
    double value = model->computeShadowing(d3D, d2D, los, link);
    return value / omnetpp::normal(snapshot.rng(), 0, 1);
};

CaseRecorder probe(this, 1e-9);
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_sub6", {}, sigmaOf(model901, ues[0], true, true));
probe.record("t901_sigma_o2i_sub6", {}, sigmaOf(model901, ues[1], true, false));
probe.record("t873_sigma_o2i", {}, sigmaOf(model873, ues[2], true, true));
probe.record("t873_sigma_o2i", {}, sigmaOf(model873, ues[3], true, false));

%postrun-command: ../../pathloss_reference.py --grade test.out >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=4 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
